{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
In the hill country of Seir he settled
Away from his brother Jacob
His possessions were [Bb6]too great to [Cm]stay
The [Bb6]land could not sup[Cm]port them
So [Abmaj7]Esau is [Bb]Edom the [Cm]father
Of the [Abmaj7]people [Bb]in the [Cm]mountains
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Chief Magdiel Chief Iram
These were [Bb6]the chiefs of [Cm]Edom
Accord[Bb]ing to their set[Ab]tlements
In [Bb]the land they [Cm]possessed
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
From the daughters of [Bb]Canaan he took [Cm]wives
[Bb]Adah and O[Cm]holiba[Bb]mah
Base[Ab]math the sister [Bb]of Nebaioth
[Cm]Born in [Bb]the land [Cm]of Ca[Ab]naan
Eliphaz and Reuel were [Bb]born
To his [Ab]children [Bb]in the [Cm]hills
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Chief Mag[Bb]diel Chief I[Cm]ram
These [Bb]were the chiefs [Cm]of Edom
Ac[Bb]cording to their [Ab]settlements
[Bb]In the land [Cm]they possessed
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Timna [Bb]Alvah [Cm]and Jetheth
Oholibamah [Bb]Elah [Cm]Pinon
Kenaz [Bb]Teman [Ab]Mibzar
Named in the [Bb]family history
[Ab]Before Israel had [Bb]kings
[Ab]Edom [Bb]had its [Cm]chiefs
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Chief [Bb]Magdiel Chief I[Cm]ram
These were [Bb]the chiefs of [Cm]Edom
Accord[Bb]ing to their set[Ab]tlements
In [Bb]the land they [Cm]possessed
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Ab]This was Esau
The father of the [Bb]Edo[Cm]mites
{end_of_verse}
